# htxdev.db is TEMPORARILY ignored, as of 2026-09-17.
#
# It is meant to be committed, and the architecture depends on that: it is the
# permanent record of every event ever seen, first_seen cannot be rebuilt from
# feeds because feeds only publish what is current, and Phase 7's GitHub
# Actions cron has no persistent state, so from that phase onward the file has
# to be in git for a sync to build on the last one. Measured at roughly 30 MB
# per year at ten sources, which is the reason that is affordable.
#
# Held back for now because it contains HLUG's private calendar entries. Their
# public Google Calendar carries "Family visit" and "Dental" alongside real
# group events, and while the pending gate keeps those off the website, it does
# nothing about a git object: `strings htxdev.db` prints them. Nothing needs
# this file committed before Phase 7, so the decision waits until the repo's
# public/private status is settled. Committing it and going public later means
# rewriting every SHA to undo, which has already been declined once here.
#
# Two rules that keep it cheap once it does land: never VACUUM in CI, because
# rewriting the whole file defeats git's delta compression, and set a
# concurrency group on the sync workflow so two runs cannot both commit it.
htxdev.db
